      "title": "THE m = 2 DECOMPOSITION GRAPH OF A PRIME-ORDER CURVE IS A PATH, SO THE RANDOM-BASE p_exist HAS AN EXACT CLOSED FORM WITH NO HEURISTIC IN IT: for every target R != O, the on-curve x-classes ordered by j in x([j] R/2) form one Hamiltonian path with a loop at x(R/2), a 2-decomposition of R over V is exactly an induced edge (or the loop vertex) of V in that path, and for a uniformly random base of size B P[R decomposes] = 1 - C(n - B, B) / C(n, B) with n = (N - 1)/2, for every curve of prime order N and every R -- which replaces the reported HEUR-SEMAEV-2015-4.3 reference curve of the frozen protocol by a theorem, predicts every cell of the ladder to four digits before any run, and brackets the m = 3 law rigorously with Janson's inequality",
