      "title": "SAMPLE THE DECOMPOSITION, NOT THE TARGET: the size-biased fibre identity #{R : c(R) >= 1} = sum over multisets M of 1/c(sum M) turns every planted sum into an informative sample, so coverage AND additive energy come from one stream at O(B^{floor(m/2)}) per sample with NO rare-event penalty -- an unbiased estimator that beats the frozen protocol's sampled-target instrument by a variance-per-cost factor of about 8/mu^2, is dominated by exact enumeration only while B^m fits the budget, and gives the lane a validation route beyond the enumeration wall inside the 32-bit cap",
