      "title": "THE PROTOCOL'S IID TRIAL MODEL IS A STATEMENT ABOUT A CAYLEY GRAPH NOBODY HAS LOOKED AT: a relation collector that re-randomises by adding factor-base elements walks on Cay(Z/N, log W), whose spectral gap is EXACT at toy scale (an FFT of the log indicator) and whose random-base value sqrt(ln(N/2)/B) is what Alon-Roichman's c_eps log|G| threshold imitates -- so at the ladder's small-B cells (B = 8, N = 4099: lambda_2 about 0.98, mixing time about 400 steps against an IID hitting time of 30) the walk-driven hit process is predicted to violate the protocol's Bernoulli model by a computable margin, and at B = 48 to obey it; the autocorrelation of the hit indicator is predicted EXACTLY from the spectrum of 1_{mW}, with an AP-in-logs base as the planted non-mixer",
